From 3f45b963dfaed63454cc9e609979bac3cdd340e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Felix <52862870+devilAPI@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:29:32 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] leds: add torch mode of the Qualcomm PMI8994/PMI8996
 flash LED module

Mainline leds-qcom-flash does not know the older PMI8994 flash module
(type 0x18, subtype 1/2). This small driver does its torch mode only,
with the register sequence of the downstream qpnp-flash-led torch path
(msm-3.18): unlock + torch mode, per-LED current (16 steps up to
200 mA), module enable, headroom sense, software strobe; and the
reverse to switch off. Both LEDs of a dual module are one LED class
device. The module takes a new current only on strobe, so a change
while lit switches off and on.

PMI8994 node (SID 3, 0xd300); Axon 7: white:torch. Tested: on/off at
levels 10 and 16, registers as downstream, no LED fault status.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
